From eb4af3affec8d1cb12195b0a4211032c263a9881 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Graham <scott.github@h4ck3r.net>
Date: Tue, 3 Mar 2026 20:38:40 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 18/18] Add experimental direct win32 .obj emission

With `-f pecoff`, directly emits a Win32 .obj rather than .s.

Output .obj should always be the same as if .s is assembled as verified
by tools/pecobjtest.sh. Tests pass, but there's probably things to do.
Some minor differences are smoothed over by the test harness (nop-style,
etc) because x86 encoding is so, uh, "flexible".
